      "side": 1,
      "message": "youre right, thanks for pointing this out. I was thinking of adding code to gracefully re-privilege the cpus on reboot shutdown and then call this, but did not get to this. I have code in v2 to re-privilege cpus if the deprivilege partially failed, but did not plug this in yet. I am thinking of doing `x86_platform.iommu_shutdown \u003d intel_iommu_shutdown;` for CONFIG_PKVM_INTEL as well for now in v2.",
